{
  "id": "cs-kraje-okresy-iso",
  "name": "České kraje a okresy s ISO 3166-2 kódy a vícejazyčnými názvy",
  "title": "České kraje a okresy s ISO 3166-2 kódy a vícejazyčnými názvy",
  "description": "Administrative subdivisions of the Czech Republic extracted from the openpotato/openholidaysapi.data monorepo (which seeds the OpenHolidays public API). Two category levels in a single dataset: 14 top-level units (13 kraje + 1 hlavní město Praha) and 76 okresy (districts) parented to their kraj via the `parent_short_name` field. Each record carries the openpotato composite code (CZ-XX), the official ISO 3166-2 subdivision code, the openpotato two-letter ShortName, the category (kraj / okres / hlavní město) in CS/EN/DE, and parallel names in Czech (default), English, and German. Complements pre-existing cs-kraje (data.gov.cz INSPIRE seed, CS only, NUTS3 codes, 14 records) and cs-okresy (separate slug) by adding both levels in a single joinable table plus German names (used in OpenHolidays cross-border documentation) and verified ISO 3166-2 references. Parent linkage uses the two-letter ShortName (e.g., okres 'BN' → parent 'ST' = Středočeský kraj).",
  "category": "geography",
  "source": "",
  "source_url": "",
